Since $\mu=0$, we have $P(X > 2)=P(X < -2)=0.023$.

Now, we want to find $P(-2\leqslant X\leqslant 2)$. Because the normal distribution is symmetric around its mean, we can rewrite the probability as follows:

\begin{align*}
P(-2\leqslant X\leqslant 2) &= P(X < 2) - P(X < -2)\\
&= 1 - P(X > 2) - P(X < -2)\\
&= 1 - 2 \times P(X > 2) \qquad \text{(due to symmetry)}\\
&= 1 - 2 \times 0.023\\
&= \boxed{0.954}
\end{align*}

